# Case presentation layering (UWorld-style)

Learner-facing cases follow **progressive disclosure** — same pattern as standard CCS cases (e.g. "Blood In Urine" + bay location only at entry).

## Play dock (default)

| Surface | Shows |
|--------|--------|
| **Header** | `presentationTitle` or chief complaint only + location (ER / OBS / ICU / WARD) |
| **Orders tab (default)** | Stacks — drag to patient. No HPI wall of text. |
| **HPI tab** | Full practice HPI when learner clicks clipboard-pulse icon |
| **Exam tab** | Physical exam when learner clicks stethoscope |
| **Thread / results** | Only after those tabs are opened |

## Spoiler bans (learning mode)

- No composite uber titles (`Robert — MSK Pain Marathon`) in learner UI
- No `— emergency presentation` stub lines as HPI
- No `briefingNote`, segment list, diagnosis, or objective until teach mode / case complete

## Data

- **Uber:** `presentationTitle` in `src/data/uberCases.json` (UWorld-style chief complaint header)
- **Internal title:** `title` field stays for teach mode / catalog authoring
- **Full story:** `uberCaseExtensions.json` `hpiNarrative` → `practice_hpi` at play time

## Code

- `learnerFacingCaseTitle()` → `learnerPresentationTitle()` in learning mode
- `getBriefingHpi()` / `resolvePracticeHpi()` reject placeholder stubs
- Teach mode: full composite title + segment labels OK
